  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Numerous showers and some embedded thunder are\nmoving thru the area and may bring locally over 2 inches of \nrain and some areas of flash flooding into early Sunday.\n\nRadar playing out the forecast very nicely. Much of the heavy\nrain has confined itself to PBZ's area, as expected. Have not\nseen any 1\"+ amounts on any buckets across our CWA, and FFG is \nhigher than that. It is good that we have the flood watch out,\nbut we may be able to start trimming it off as this push of rain\ngoes past. HRRR and RAP had been different on the timing of \nrain exit from the watch area, but are now both languishing rain\nover the CWA much of the night - just light rain, though. Thus\nfar, we have had no hydro issues, and the threat seems to be\ncoming to a close. But some training of 0.5-0.75\" rainfall is\nseen over the NW at this time. That will add onto the 0.25-0.5\"\nwe had at first late this aftn. But, it still looks fairly tame\nor even of no consequence. Will allow the watch to continue as\nis for the time being. But, we may be able to drop it earlier\nthan 08Z (curr exp time).",
